ngp: compile Sass component styles (.scss/.sass, inlineStyleLanguage)

ngtsc leaves stylesheet preprocessing to its resource host (the Angular CLI's
transformResource); ngp ran without one and inlined Sass verbatim, so `$vars`,
mixins and @use reached the browser. ngp now applies the Angular CLI rules:

- styleUrl(s) and template <link> stylesheets compile by extension
  (.scss -> SCSS, .sass -> indented syntax, other files untouched);
- inline `styles` use angular.json `inlineStyleLanguage`
  (or `--inline-style-language css|scss|sass`);
- angular.json `stylePreprocessorOptions.includePaths` and the workspace
  node_modules are Sass load paths;
- `sass` is resolved from the workspace, loaded only when needed;
- a stylesheet that does not compile is reported as NG2008 (like a stylesheet
  ngtsc cannot load), with the Sass message, anchored on its styleUrl.

Applies to Angular 22.3.0-rc.0 and 22.3.0, packages/compiler-cli/preprocessor.

